---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { createBreadcrumbSchema } from '~/utils/structured-data';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Engineering Content and Editorial Policy',
  description:
    'How COPPER 3DP prepares, reviews, sources, labels, and updates engineering content about copper additive manufacturing.',
  structuredData: createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', item: '/' },
    { name: 'Engineering content policy', item: '/editorial-policy/' },
  ]),
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:py-20">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary">Trust and methodology</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-heading sm:text-5xl">
        Engineering content and editorial policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
        COPPER 3DP publishes practical guidance for engineers and buyers evaluating copper additive manufacturing. The
        purpose is to support informed process, material, inspection, and quotation decisions before production files
        are submitted.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-10 max-w-none dark:prose-invert dark:prose-headings:text-heading prose-a:text-link">
      <h2>Who prepares the content</h2>
      <p>
        Articles are published under <strong>COPPER 3DP Engineering</strong>. Content is prepared from project
        requirements, supplier process capability, manufacturing constraints, and public technical sources relevant to
        copper LPBF and finished copper components. Commercial inquiries and production coordination are handled by
        Suzhou Como Precision Materials Co., Ltd.
      </p>

      <h2>How technical claims are handled</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Material and process claims should be tied to a named material route, condition, or source where practical.
        </li>
        <li>
          Property values are not presented as universal guarantees for every machine, build, orientation, or finished
          part.
        </li>
        <li>
          Application pages separate printable geometry from post-processing, inspection, and functional acceptance.
        </li>
        <li>
          External sources provide technical context; customer-specific acceptance criteria still come from the drawing
          and quotation requirements.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cases, scenarios, and evidence</h2>
      <p>
        A named customer result is only described as a customer case when publication rights and supporting evidence are
        available. Otherwise, a page may use an <strong>illustrative design-review scenario</strong> to explain a common engineering
        decision. Those scenarios are labeled and must not be read as claims about a specific customer, machine run, measured
        result, or production program.
      </p>

      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>
        Images are used when they identify a real component type, expose internal geometry, explain a failure mode, or
        clarify an inspection decision. Decorative image count is not a publishing target. A page may use one
        representative image or no additional diagrams when text and tables answer the search task more clearly.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Substantive revisions receive an updated date. Dates are not changed merely to make content appear fresh. Pages
        may be consolidated or redirected when several URLs answer the same engineering question, when a newer page is
        more complete, or when an old page no longer supports a reliable engineering decision.
      </p>

      <h2>What the content does not replace</h2>
      <p>
        Website guidance is not a manufacturing guarantee, certified material report, simulation, safety assessment, or
        acceptance plan for a specific part. A quotation requires the CAD model, drawing, quantity, operating
        requirements, material preference if known, and the inspection or documentation scope that matters.
      </p>

      <p>
        Corrections and technical questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@szcomo.com">info@szcomo.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
